re managing people yet or  not for the people who are above you you  have to earn their trust so think about  your boss for them to trust you you have  to earn it you can't just say hey trust  me I'll get it done when people say  trust me you know you don't really tend  to want to trust them so you have you  have to earn it right Trust has to be  earned so whenever they give you a  project try to go above and beyond do it  faster than they expect do it higher  quality than xpect think of other ways  to make the project better  just what your you've been assigned and  you'll be the one on your team that  everybody trusts because you always do a  really good job so you have to earn that  and think of ways that you can always go  above and beyond to earn their trust in  this if you have a business it's the  same thing to earn the trust of your  customers can't say hey trust me you  have to prove to them that you're going  to over-deliver on expectations you  deliver it faster cheaper better then  you said you would and you're going to  earn a lifetime of trust from them if  you're managing people and you worried  about earning the trust of the people  below you show them trust first but if  you can show that you trust them they're  going to want to trust you so try not to  be a big micromanager I try not to  breathe down their necks and really push  them on timelines yes you have to get  their job done but try not to be  overbearing to the point where they feel  like you don't trust them if you show  that you do trust them then they're  probably going to work even harder  you'll probably be surprised by how hard  they were and they're going to start  trusting you as well and it's going to  help the entire company so I hope that  answer your question if you guys liked  the video please give it a thumbs up  below and I'd also love to hear your  thoughts and feedback if you want to  leave a comment below the video and stay  tuned to the next episode  you
 

